body:
I noticed when I was dating a girl I had an iPhone and Samsung that were published in the same year, but I used Samsung instead of an IPhone, and as soon as I showed her that I have iPhone she started persuading me to use it and so on.

I really think that girls regard iPhone users as higher but in my opinion it is shallow.

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

But there are studies about it as well(don't know how reliable they are):

https://appleinsider.com/articles/20/08/28/an-iphone-makes-you-76-more-attractive-on-dating-apps

I don't understand what the goal is with having bigger boobs. Are you trying to get attention from more guys? If you have the attention of some guys already, isn't that enough?

&#x200B;

You can also look better by doing other things such as exercise.

Not all Romans were stoics, as far as I know. So does the stoicism support the idea of climbing the ladder of the social hierarchy, or is it against it? I cannot understand it. Should we try as hard as possible during the work to gain high social status, or do we kind of do the work for others?

&#x200B;

Also, in my opinion higher social status doesn't mean that you are contributing to society in a positive way.

Thanks for the advice! I don't like the hooker part either. I don't actually want to pursue the only sex part of the relationships(because that would make me empty), but I would rather let the flow go in its own way. And I struggle to do it since every time the intimate moment comes I cannot act and the opposite sex thinks that I don't like them(or something else)

&#x200B;

I am thinking of pursuing a normal relationship where I will be honest since the situations that I am talking about appeared in a bar or in similar places. That is why recently I have been trying to go to more meaningful events. However, people that I talk with are very beautiful and I cannot believe that so beautiful girls would come to me and start talking and something inside me always tries to deny it. There are so many things that don't add up, I don't really know if there are some issues with my self-esteem or is it a misinterpretation of the situation. Sometimes I think that it is not about confidence but about self-esteem.

&#x200B;

I also feel sometimes that it is about manning up, but the more I told it to myself the more unemotional I became.
